<% content_for :title, "Privacy policy" %>

<article class="w-full max-w-2xl rounded-xl bg-white p-8 shadow-md">
  <p class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-red-700 uppercase">Ruby on Rails Demo by Isara Nakavisute</p>
  <h1 class="mb-1 text-2xl font-bold">Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="mb-6 text-sm text-gray-500">Last updated: <%= l Date.new(2026, 10, 3), format: :long %></p>

  <div class="grid gap-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-700 [&_h2]:mb-1 [&_h2]:text-base [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-gray-900 [&_li]:ml-5 [&_li]:list-disc">
    <section>
      <p>This website is a demonstration project. This page explains what information it stores about you and how it is used.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Information we store</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your account:</strong> your username and password.</li>
        <li><strong>Two-factor authentication:</strong> the secret used by your authenticator app (stored encrypted) and your recovery codes (stored only in a scrambled, one-way form).</li>
        <li><strong>If you sign in with Google or Facebook:</strong> your Google or Facebook account ID, and the name and email address they share with us. We use your email address only to suggest your username.</li>
        <li><strong>Sign-in records:</strong> the date, your IP address and browser type for each sign-in, and for any “Forgot password” request.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We don't post anything to your Google or Facebook account, or read your contacts, photos or messages.</li>
        <li>We don't sell or share your information with anyone, and we don't use it for advertising.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>Only to let you sign in, keep your account secure (including two-factor authentication and protection against automated sign-in attempts), and run the shop on this website.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="data-deletion">
      <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
      <p>To remove the connection to Google or Facebook, sign in and go to <strong>Account</strong>, then click <strong>Disconnect</strong>. You can also remove this app's access from your Google account (Security &rarr; Third-party access) or Facebook (Settings &rarr; Apps and websites).</p>
      <p class="mt-2">To delete your whole account and all information stored about it, contact the administrator of this website. It will be deleted within 30 days.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be published on this page with a new date.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-8 text-center text-sm">
    <%= link_to "← Back to sign in", login_path, class: "text-red-700 hover:underline" %>
  </p>
</article>
